From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maksim Sisov <msisov@igalia.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:11:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/48] extensions: Warn about mime_types_handler at install

An extension can declare the mime_types_handler manifest key and become
the handler for every PDF the user opens. Today this shows no permission
warning, neither at install nor when an update adds the key.

Make the key a permission. The install prompt and the update check now
show "Read and display PDF files" for it. Allowlisted handlers are not
affected. Extensions that already have the key are disabled on the next
start until the user approves.

      unit_tests --gtest_filter='PermissionsTest.IsPrivilegeIncrease:
      PermissionMessageCombinationsUnittest.MimeTypesHandler*:
      ExtensionServiceTest.MimeTypesHandler*'
Manual Test: install an extension with the key and see the prompt,
             update an extension to a version that adds the key and
             see it disabled.

Test: extensions_unittests --gtest_filter='MimeTypesHandler*'
